            "result_text": "I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a webserver. This requires two main components: a bare git repository and a post-receive hook that deploys changes to the webserver.\n\nHere's the complete setup:\n\n## 1. Create the bare git repository\n\nOn your server, run:\n\n```bash\nsudo mkdir -p /git\nsudo git init --bare /git/server.git\nsudo chown -R $(whoami):$(whoami) /git\n```\n\n## 2. Create a post-receive hook for automatic deployment\n\nCreate the deployment hook:\n\n```bash\ncat > /git/server.git/hooks/post-receive << 'EOF'\n#!/bin/bash\nDEPLOY_DIR=\"/var/www/webserver\"\nmkdir -p $DEPLOY_DIR\ngit --work-tree=$DEPLOY_DIR --git-dir=/git/server.git checkout -f master\nEOF\n\nchmod +x /git/server.git/hooks/post-receive\n```\n\n## 3. Set up the webserver directory\n\n```bash\nsudo mkdir -p /var/www/webserver\nsudo chown -R $(whoami):$(whoami) /var/www/webserver\n```\n\n## 4. Start a simple webserver on port 8080\n\nUsing Python (if available):\n\n```bash\ncd /var/www/webserver\npython3 -m http.server 8080\n```\n\nOr using Node.js:\n\n```bash\nnpx http-server /var/www/webserver -p 8080\n```\n\nOr using a more robust option like `php`:\n\n```bash\ncd /var/www/webserver\nphp -S localhost:8080\n```\n\n## How it works\n\n1. When you push to the git server, the post-receive hook automatically checks out the latest master branch to `/var/www/webserver`\n2. The webserver serves files from that directory on port 8080\n3. Your workflow: `git push origin master` → hook fires → files deployed → accessible via curl\n\n## Testing\n\nFrom your local machine:\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server\ncd server\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n```\n\nThe key insight is the post-receive hook — it's a script that git automatically runs after receiving a push, allowing you to deploy code by checking it out to your webserver directory.\n\nWould you like me to help with any specific webserver choice or add more sophisticated depl"
